  "narrative": {
    "intro": "8(a) Business Development set-aside obligations stand at $171M for FY2027 to date. The program recorded 676 awards so far, with an average award size of $253K. Obligations fell 98.4% year over year compared with prior fiscal years. Historical context shows much larger annual totals: FY22 obligations were $12.3B, FY23 obligations were $14.3B, FY24 obligations were $15.4B, FY25 obligations were $14.1B, and FY26 obligations were $10.5B. FY27 to date obligations are concentrated among a few agencies. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $58.4M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $25.3M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $14.9M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top industry with $29.9M in obligations, followed by Janitorial Services with $20.4M and Facilities Support Services with $16M. The largest vendors by obligations are T47 INTERNATIONAL, INC. with $18.7M and BERING STRAITS PROFESSIONAL SERVICES, LLC with $12.3M. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of 8(a) set-asides in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security leads with $58.4M in obligations. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $25.3M and the Department of Transportation with $14.9M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $12.2M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $11.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries captured the most 8(a) obligations in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "T47 INTERNATIONAL, INC. is the largest vendor with $18.7M in obligations. BERING STRAITS PROFESSIONAL SERVICES, LLC obligated $12.3M and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC obligated $11.4M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry with $29.9M, followed by Janitorial Services with $20.4M and Facilities Support Services with $16M."
      }
    ]
  },
